FerrionOS change to the upstream installer (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 16d39fe1f20f15fc97fa3aaa216ac7e449637d41 after the existing recipe patches.

One password: disk encryption is modeled explicitly by DiskEncryption (Off | Password { secret, unlock_account }) and GUI Encryption (Off | On { account, password, confirm }), validated through TryFrom<&GeneralConfig> and matched once in DiskOption. The text and graphical installers ask for an account name and one password, write /etc/unlock-slots (mode 0600, root) and EFI/BOOT/UNLOCK.TXT, skip the fast clone, and strip encrypt_disk, unlock_account and the unlock account's password from the installed filesystem.toml.

